# Summon the Blackguard's Fiendish Servant and look at what turns up. That is
# bd inc-tek.8.3 finding PA-03-F15: the effect summoned a babau, which is
# neither of the two creatures its own description names, and gave it a
# finite duration although the description says twice that it stays until
# dismissed.
#
# WHY THERE IS NO BLACKGUARD HERE. The ability arrives at Blackguard 5. The
# class gate wants a base attack bonus of +6 and Knowledge (Infernal) 8, and
# no class with a 100%% attack rate carries that skill, so entry costs eight
# core levels. Eight plus five is thirteen, in a game that stops at eleven
# (MAX_CHAR_LEVEL, inc/Defines.h:4367). No character can hold the ability.
#
# WHAT IS DONE INSTEAD. The class grants it as
#   Ability[CA_INNATE_SPELL,$"fiendish servant"] at 5th level
# (lib/prestige.irh:852), so the thing being tested is an effect that a
# creature casts, not a passive the class computes. Wizard mode's Learn Any
# Spell takes a resource name, checks it is a T_TEFFECT and marks it
# SP_KNOWN|SP_PRIMAL|SP_INNATE (src/Debug.cpp:850-863). That is the same
# state the class grant produces, reached without the class.
#
# THE ORACLE is the creature that appears. A babau is a CR 6 demon; a true
# imp is the imp the description names. The name is printed on the map's
# Things in View panel and in the summoning message.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Human"
@choose "Knowledge (Infernal)"  # humans choose two bonus skills
@while "Choose a skill:" a
@choose "Warrior"
a                               # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
@choose "Neutral"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a  # the warrior's free Weapon Focus
@while "Choose a feat" a
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
# The screen will not close while a rank is unspent. Eight of them, two to a
# skill; which skills does not matter here.
@cursorto:mark "Athletics" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Bluff" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Climb" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Craft" DOWN
RIGHT*2
ENTER y

a                               # Personality archetype
ESC                             # dismiss the arrival-room description
w                               # wizard mode
y
@dump:wizmenu
w                               # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE                           # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

# The effect is cast at the caster's level, and "Nothing happens." is what a
# level 1 caster gets: the summon's own pval is 6. The blackguard who would
# really hold it is 13th level by the time he does, so the character is taken
# to the cap.
d
@dump:sheet0
G
@dump:afterG
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" c
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "Unspent Skill Ranks" ESC
G
